# <%= module %> — instructions for coding agents

Generated by `mix samen.gen.app`. Read this before changing anything; the gate is the oracle.

## The gate

    MIX_ENV=test bash ci.sh

Run it after EVERY change, in the foreground (do not background it and poll).
It must end `<%= otp_app %> CI gate: ALL PASSED`. It runs compile (`--warnings-as-errors`), the
`schema.dict.json` drift check, the `samen.verify.*` verifiers, the default tests and the vault
anti-tautology probe. Steps are numbered in its output; a failing step prints the verifier's message.

## When a verifier fails

Every failure message is indexed (error string -> verifier -> meaning -> fix) in the framework repo's
`<%= samen_core_path %>/../docs/guides/gate-failures.md`. Look the message up there first. Short version:

- `schema.dict.json is stale` — you changed a resource or migration; re-baseline with
  `mix samen.catalog.dump --output schema.dict.json` and commit it (revert instead if the change was unintended).
- `catalog_parity`, `migrations` — a migration must `use Samen.Migration` and call `catalog_sync(@resources)`.
- `prefixes`, `abbrev` errors — a column or abbrev does not follow the registry (see hands-off rules).
- `pii_*`, `no_plaintext_pii`, `vault_declared_parity` — a PII field is not declared and routed through the vault.
- `same_org_fk`, `tnt_*`, `aggregate_privacy` — tenant isolation: add the same-org check; never widen a mount.
- `api_contract` — a structural break to `/api/v1` (removed field, dropped route); additive changes are fine.

## Hands-off rules (never do these to turn the gate green)

- NEVER add or edit rows in `<%= samen_core_path %>/priv/abbrev_registry.json` by hand. Reserve abbrevs only with
  `mix samen.abbrev.reserve --host <%= otp_app %> --abbrev <abc> --owner <Module>` (or the `mix samen.gen.*` tasks).
  Abbrevs are permanent and never recycled.
- PII is written ONLY through governed actions on a resource's `pii do ... end` fields (vault-routed, masked
  `••••` by default). Never store plaintext in a plain attribute, never read a `vt_*` token as a value, never
  bypass `Samen.Api.PiiResolution` or hand-mask.
- NEVER weaken a verifier, delete a test, edit the committed `schema.dict.json` or `api_contract.v1.json` by hand,
  or add an allow-list entry to make a gate pass. Fix the cause.
- An unconfigured adapter returns `{:error, :not_configured}`, never a fake `{:ok, _}`.

## Common tasks

- Add a resource: `mix samen.gen.resource --scope <Scope> --resource <Name> --abbrev <abc> [--live]` (add
  `mix samen.gen.scope --scope <Scope>` first for a new scope). It writes the resource, migration, tests and
  registry row. Then `MIX_ENV=test mix ecto.migrate`, `mix samen.catalog.dump --output schema.dict.json`, and
  (if the resource is exposed on the API) `mix samen.verify.api_contract --version v1 --update`.
- Add a field: there is no generator. Edit the resource, write a migration (`use Samen.Migration`, end `up/0`
  with `catalog_sync(@resources)`), run it, then re-dump `schema.dict.json`. A PII field goes in the resource's
  `pii do` block and must have a masking test (plane-clear, plane-masked, and a leak-detected twin).
- Add an agent: `mix samen.gen.agent --scope <Scope> --name <Name> [--tools a,b]`.
- Every generator refuses unknown flags and refuses to overwrite; there is no dry-run, so read the task's
  `mix help samen.gen.<kind>` before running it.

## Where things are

- Schema dictionary (ground truth for table/column/PII names): `schema.dict.json`. Ground on it before
  writing code; `mix samen.catalog.dump --domain <Domain>` dumps one domain.
- Public API contract (apps with the default JSON:API surface): `api_contract.v1.json`, the `/api/v1`
  surface, deny-by-default.
- Framework docs: `<%= samen_core_path %>/../docs/` (guides, ADRs, `docs/guides/llm-grounding.md`).
